∇ ret← {modBits} GmpzExample secret_msg
⍝  A nice example of gmpz in operation: RSA encoding of a "secret" message.
⍝  To run:
⍝    GmpzExample secret_msg
⍝  Choose a secret message to encode using a private and public key.
⍝  Here everything else is done for you. 
⍝  You can also change the modBits from the default (1024) to 2048 or 4096.
⍝
⍝  Note: The message must be smaller than the key size (everything in bits).
⍝        Bigger messages are best handled through combining the RSA message with another
⍝        faster method (using the RSA message to encode the keys for that method).

⍝--1 DECLARATIONS AND INITIALIZATION ------------------------------------------------------------------
⍝  Declarations, definitions, etc.
⍝  Declare helper functions
     ; HS; Tidy
⍝  Declare all mpz_t variables
     ; p; q; n; phi; e; eN; d; msg; cipher; decrypted

⍝  Be sure gmpz is loaded...
   :IF 0= #.⎕NC 'gmpz'
       #.⎕FIX 'gmpz/gmpz.dyalog'
   :EndIf 
⍝  Define helper fn HS (Unicode => hexadecimal String)
⍝  HS:    str@CV← [[1: encrypt | 0: decrypt]] ∇ str@CV
   HS← {⎕IO← 0 ⋄ ⍺← 1 ⋄ hd← ⎕D,'abcdef' ⋄ U← 'UTF-8'∘⎕UCS
     ⍺=1: ,hd[⍉16 16⊤U ⍵] ⋄ U 16⊥hd⍳⍉t⍴⍨2,⍨2÷⍨≢t← ⎕C ⍵~' '
   }
⍝  Define helper fn Tidy: Print long results in nice rows of 64 bytes, with left margin of  4 spaces
⍝  Tidy:    ∇ str@CV
   Tidy← 64 { ⍺← ⍬ ⋄ p← ⍵⍵⍴'' ⋄ ⍺⍺≥ ≢⍵: ↑⍺,⊂p, ⍵ ⋄ (⍺, ⊂p, ⍺⍺↑⍵) ∇ ⍺⍺↓⍵ } 4

⍝  Initialize all mpz variables
   p q n phi e d msg cipher decrypted← gmpz.New¨9⍴0

⍝  Initialise modBits: max # of bits in the modulus.  Must be even.
   :IF 900⌶⍬
       modBits← 1024                                            ⍝ Best practices: modBits∊ 2048 4096
   :EndIf 
   'Modulus must be even number of bits' ⎕SIGNAL 11/⍨ 0≠ 2|modBits

⍝--2 GENERATE PUBLIC AND PRIVATE KEYS -----------------------------------------------------------------
⍝  Initialize random number generator with entropy
⍝     (automatic/default when RandB is first called)
⍝   Generate two distinct 512-bit probable primes (p and q)

⍝  p...
   p.(NextPrime RandB) modBits÷2

⍝  q...
   :Repeat  ⍝⍝ Ensure p ≠ q
      q.(NextPrime RandB) modBits÷2
   :Until q.Ne p

⍝  Compute the  modulus n: n ← p × q, where n.BitLen is approx modBits (may be a bit smaller)
   p n.Mul q

⍝  Compute Euler's totient: phi← (p - 1) × (q - 1)
   p.Dec phi.Mul q.Dec                                       ⍝ p is now p-1, q is now q-1

⍝  Set public exponent e = 65537 and compute private exponent
   eN← 65537   
   e.Set eN 
   :If 0=e d.Invert phi                                      ⍝ Invert: d← e*-1 mod phi
      ret← 'Error: e and phi are not coprime.'  ⋄ :Return
   :EndIf

⍝- 3 IMPORT MSG -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
⍝  Import the plaintext secret_msg ==> msg, where secret_msg will be encoded via UTF-8 for simplicity.
   16 msg.Set HS secret_msg

   :If msg.BitLen≥ n.BitLen                                  ⍝ length limited for demo...
      ret← 'Your message is too big' ⋄  :Return
   :EndIf

⍝--4 ENCRYPT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
⍝  Encrypt: cipher ← (msg * e) mod n
   msg cipher.PowM e n

⍝--5 DECRYPT -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
⍝  Decrypt: decrypted ← (cipher * d) mod n
   cipher decrypted.PowM d n

⍝--6 PRINT AND VERIFY-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
⍝  Print results--- Key elements are in Base 62 for brevity.
    '' 
    'Public Key Modulus    (n)  ' ⋄  Tidy n.GetInBase 62               ⋄   '' 
    'Public Key Exponent   (e) '  ⋄  Tidy e.GetInBase 62               ⋄   '' 
    'Private Key Exponent  (d) '  ⋄  Tidy d.GetInBase 62               ⋄   '' 
    'Encrypted Message'           ⋄  Tidy cipher.GetInBase 62          ⋄   '' 
    'Decrypted Message'           ⋄  Tidy 0 HS decrypted.GetInBase 16  ⋄   '' 
⍝  Verify correctness
   :If 0=msg.Cmp decrypted
      ret← '🙂🙂🙂 Success: Decrypted message matches original'
   :Else
      ret← '😖😖😖 Failure: Decrypted message does not match original'
   :EndIf

⍝--7 CLEAN UP / FREE MEMORY ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
⍝  Free all allocated memory
⍝  gmpz does it all for you!
⍝  (i.e. there's nothing for you to do.)
 
⍝--8 TEST RUN (abridged) --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
⍝ GmpzExample '🐱 This is a cat 🐱'  
⍝ 
⍝ Public Key Modulus    (n)  
⍝     Lo8ZzLofubJlwMYj3GhaW6cytVYNk4RzJzrJGNAeT8PDnxHisJnaHwRBo1wiZXPd...                  
⍝
⍝ Public Key Exponent   (e) 
⍝     H33
⍝
⍝ Private Key Exponent  (d) 
⍝     HBpcPxScN3WQo0vh8GopYjNSqceMnzOsG0SZo7x7hPwymp3a04M8ikDrGUwwNVJK...                   
⍝
⍝ Encrypted Message
⍝     73jaAzZZBfu0dWBQE14O7qnX12eBzhgumcESOsnx6RcH7cPdzWibgpN6munVdLIq...                   
⍝
⍝ Decrypted Message
⍝     🐱 This is a cat 🐱
⍝
⍝ 🙂🙂🙂 Success: Decrypted message matches original